English:
Survivor Log, Entry 1
@w2 Ensign Caplin managed to evade the alien drones that were chasing us. @w2 Unfortunately, we don't have anywhere to go. @w2 This Module can't go into warp, @w1 obviously, @w1 and we'd never survive an atmospheric entry, @w1 let alone crash landing on the planet. @w2 Ensign Caplin suggested we try to find a nearby asteroid where we can set up a temporary base with the stuff we brought from the Cargo Module. 

@p9 I could probably set up the Ventilator easy enough, @w2 and transfer the computer terminals into a pocket of the asteroid. @w2 I'm not so sure we can survive very long, @w1 unless we can either find a small vessel of some kind, @w1 or one of the other ships from the fleet finds us. @w2 I guess we'll see.
@w4 -Engineer Cardenas

Chinese (simplified):
幸存者日志，条目1
@w2 卡普林少尉设法摆脱了追赶我们的外星无人机。@w2 不幸的是，我们没有地方可去。@w2 这个模块无法进行翘曲，@w1 显然，@w1 而且我们绝不可能在大气层进入中幸存下来，@w1 更不用说在星球上坠毁了。@w2 卡普林少尉建议我们尝试寻找附近的小行星，用我们从货物模块带来的东西建立一个临时基地。

@p9 我应该能轻松安装好通风器，@w2 并把计算机终端转移到小行星的空腔里。@w2 我不太确定我们能存活很久，@w1 除非我们能找到某种小型飞船，@w1 或者舰队中的其他飞船找到我们。@w2 到时候再说吧。
@w4 ——卡德纳斯工程师

English:
Survivor Log, Entry 2
@w2 I managed to find a Magnesium Asteroid large enough to drill into and set up a base. @w2 With some skillful maneuvers, I managed to park the Cryo Module in a crevice that allowed us to begin digging out a hole. 

@p9 Engineer Cardenas says he can have the hole drilled and Ventilator set up within the hour. @w2 Once he does, @w1 Doctor Bonilla and I will begin setting up the habitat while he sets up the computer terminals. @w2 I'm probably not going to be much use from here on, @w1 but at least we're not dead yet.
@w4 -Ensign Caplin, Helmsman

