@w4 In the ancient legends of my ancestors, @w1 the Funayūrei are spirits of the dead that, @w1 among other things, @w1 possess the husks of shipwrecks and attempt to sink any other ships they come across. @w2 I never believed such things, @w1 until now.  @w2 As we approached the derelict ship, it began to glow with an unnatural green light, @w1 and came to life. @w2 Its first volley of weapons fire damaged a good portion of the hull, @w1 but I managed to evade them quickly enough to avoid a hull breach. 

