@w4 Our proximity to the Black Hole is preventing our navigation systems from getting a lock on our galactic position, @w1 and for some reason we can't see any stars other than the Black Hole itself. 

@p9 Engineer Hansley has detected some sort of strange energy being emitted from the Black Hole, @w1 which is theoretically impossible. @w2 While we may not get the chance to use the information ourselves, @w1 I've instructed the engineering crew to gather as much information as possible about the phenomenon. @w2 Perhaps someone will eventually find our ship and be able to make use of the information.
@w4 - Captain Lopez

