@p9 Engineer Log, Entry 1
@w4 This is impossible. @w2 No matter how far or fast we move, @w1 we seem to maintain a constant distance from the Black Hole. @w2 Unless our sensor data is WAY off, @w1 we're not close enough to be within the event horizon of a Black Hole of this size. @w2 Even so, @w1 if we WERE inside the event horizon, @w1 we should be being pulled apart by the gravitational forces. @w2 If we are close enough to the event horizon, @w1 we may be suffering the effects of time dilation and not even realize it. @w2 For all we know, @w1 although we've only experienced mere hours, @w1 we could have been here for tens, @w1 or even hundreds of years!
@w4 - Engineer Hansley

