@w4 It seems that we're not leaving this area any time soon. @w2 The Captain ordered us to try to warp away from the black hole. @w2 Not only did it NOT work at all, @w1 but it also drained our warp fuel completely. @w2 With nothing else left to lose, @w1 the Captain ordered us to try to fly toward the black hole. @w2 As insane as it sounded, @w1 I did as I was ordered.

@p9 Despite all logic, @w1 not to mention physics, @w1 no matter how fast we flew toward the black hole, @w1 our distance remained the same. @w2 With no other frame of reference, @w1 apart from our instruments telling us we were moving, @w1 we would have no way to know that we were actually moving. @w2 Maybe we aren't. @w2 We seem to be in some kind of locational limbo: @w2 Neither moving nor stationary.
@w4 - Ensign Ashford

